opolitical catalyst was independently verified for a timed row; retain unscheduled policy/geopolitical headlines as risk watch, not a fabricated calendar event.</li></ul></section><section style=\"background:#1a1f2e;border:1px solid #2d3748;border-radius:12px;padding:16px;margin:0 0 12px;\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#c8a97a;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.6px;margin:0 0 10px;\">Omissions and Watch</div><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:18px;color:#e2e8f0;font-size:11px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px;\">BLS direct schedule endpoint returned HTTP 403. Official BLS release-specific pages were inspectable and current for Employee Benefits, JOLTS, metro employment and the Oct 2 Employment Situation; dates/times above are sourced there. No CPI or PPI release is scheduled in this checked window.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px;\">TreasuryDirect returned bill auctions for Sep 28-29; no note, bond or FRN auction record was returned for Sep 25-Oct 2, so none is listed.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px;\">NAR&#x27;s official 2026 release schedule has no housing release in this window (next listed Oct 13). EIA series identify report dates, while the EIA schedule supplies 10:30 AM ET release time; reference weeks are not posted yet.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px;\">Snapshot market prices use a single Yahoo Finance quote source and may be indicative; labels preserve each quote&#x27;s observation time. No unsupported market quote is substituted for missing official data.</li></ul></section><section style=\"background:#1a1f2e;border:1px solid #2d3748;border-radius:12px;padding:16px;margin:0 0 12px;\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#c8a97a;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.6px;margin:0 0 10px;\">Trading Strategy Note | ES Futures</div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:9px;\"><div style=\"background:rgba(52,211,153,.07);border:1px solid rgba(52,211,153,.22);border-radius:9px;padding:12px;\"><div style=\"font-size:10px;color:#34d399;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:5px;\">BASE CASE</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:#e2e8f0;\">Treat the Sep 30 PCE/income-spending release and Oct 2 payrolls as the principal scheduled volatility windows. Today, let the 8:30 AM durable-goods details and rates response set the tone; avoid assuming a directional surprise.</div></div><div style=\"background:rgba(248,113,113,.07);border:1px solid rgba(248,113,113,.22);border-radius:9px;padding:12px;\"><div style=\"font-size:10px;color:#f87171;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:5px;\">INVALIDATION</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:#e2e8f0;\">Invalidate a range/continuation thesis if ES breaks and holds beyond the overnight range with confirmation from Treasury yields and volatility, or if data materially reprices the policy path. Scenario framework only, not a trade signal.</div></div></div></section></div>"}